  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rural Water Supply and Sanitation Project In N&apos;Zerekore Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to support the Government&apos;s efforts to enhance access to safe drinking water and sanitation in the rural areas of the Guinea Forest, specifically targeting the prefectures of N&#x2019;Zerekore, Lola, and Yomou.
The primary objective is to improve the living conditions of the population in the project area by increasing access to safe water supplies and improved sanitation.
Specific objectives include the construction of approximately 455 boreholes equipped with hand pumps and 20 mini water supply systems. Additionally, the project will involve the construction of 1,000 family latrines, the equipping of 425 public buildings with improved sanitation facilities, and the implementation of sensitization and social intermediation activities focused on sanitation and hygiene.</narrative>
  </description>
